# Force LF line endings for all data/CSV files regardless of OS or local
# git config (core.autocrlf). Without this, a script's pre-commit SHA-256
# (computed on the file as written to disk, before git ever touches it)
# can silently diverge from the hash of what git actually stores and
# hands back on any future clone/pull -- discovered 2026-08-20 during
# US500 onboarding verification (research/S1_US500_ONBOARDING_SNAPSHOT.md),
# where the script-reported hash and the git-stored hash did not match.
# This does not retroactively fix any already-committed file's hash
# claims; it only prevents new divergence going forward.
*.csv text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
